    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0914" n="877" xml:id="pg877"/>

                <head>279. Memorandum From the Deputy Assistant Secretary of Defense for
                    International Economic and Technology Affairs (Frost) to the Under Secretary of Defense for Policy (Komer)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d279-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1980-07-16">July 16, 1980</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Security Implications of the Energy Crunch</item>
                </list>
                <p>You recently asked for an analytical paper on the security implications of the
                    energy crunch<anchor n="2" xml:id="d279-f2"/> that might be sent to Under
                    Secretary Newsom, along with the cover
                    memo at Tab A.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d279-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Attached, next under, is a draft memorandum prepared by Don Goldstein that builds
                    on your earlier thoughts on this issue.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d279-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>We have coordinated the draft with Major General Boverie.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        Ellen L. Frost<anchor n="5"
                            xml:id="d279-f5"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d279-a1.xml" xpointer="d279-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d279-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d279-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, OASD/ISA Files: FRC 330–82–0263, Box 1, ASD/ISA #3 Policy Files. Secret. Sent through Assistant Secretary
                    of Defense for International Security Affairs David
                        E. McGiffert.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f2" n="2" xml:id="d279-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Komer requested the paper in a June 21
                    note to McGiffert. (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f3" n="3" xml:id="d279-f3-content">
                <p>The unsigned and undated cover memorandum from Komer to Newsom is
                    attached but not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f4" n="4" xml:id="d279-f4-content">
                <p>See, for example, <ref target="#d271">Document 271</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f5" n="5" xml:id="d279-f5-content">
                <p>
                    Frost signed “Ellen” above this typed
                    signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
